    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the info. the Kelvin-Helmholtz thing makes sense, i've actually noticed some wave-like patterns in the clouds upstairs when i'm mid-session. what about moisture content? if i'm pulling too much water from the surrounding area to force a downpour here, will that create a localized vacuum effect that might destabilize the pressure gradient? i don't want to cause a microburst by mistake.",
